Package: fovannotator
Type: Package
Title: Field-of-View Annotation for Baited Remote Underwater Video
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Brooke", "Gibbons", email = "brooke.gibbons@marineecology.io",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A 'shiny' application for measuring field-of-view covariates on
    still frames from baited remote underwater video stations (BRUVS): the
    percentage of the view that is open water column, seabed, or blocked by
    nearby structure, after excluding the bait arm and bag. Frames are
    annotated in the browser with drawing, editing, magic-wand and erase
    tools. Automatic tools estimate the seabed horizon by dynamic programming,
    locate the bait arm from its shape and colour, and train a random-forest
    pixel classifier on frames that have been reviewed. Projects can be shared
    by several annotators, every edit is logged, and results export as one
    row per frame.
